        "original_id": "984b264d-ac5a-5cc4-b9df-e69e00fdd550",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Greenery Day\n- People: Emperor Shōwa, Hirohito\n- Places: Japan\n- Concepts: national holidays, names\n\nFacts:\n- During the Shōwa era, Japan celebrated Emperor Shōwa's birthday on April 29 every year.\n- The present observance of Greenery Day as a national holiday in Japan stems from the celebration of Emperor Shōwa's birthday on April 29.\n- Hirohito is the personal name of Emperor Shōwa.\n- The name Hirohito means \"abundant benevolence\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
